[Music]  with global event 2 now in full swing  has become very apparent that a lot of  people were just not very prepared for  the new close combat modifiers most of  the match made missions have played last  night were far more difficult than they  should have been with modifiers like  crucial and major assault having a  downed agent or two can quickly cause  the whole team to wipe and for this  reason I was actually finding more  success in running missions solo with  the right build this event is actually a  hell of a lot of fun but you really need  to understand the event modifiers when  selecting the right pieces a couple of  weeks ago I released a video on what we  know about the global event assaults in  summary assault is all about close range  but not just that you'll do considerably  more damage at close range but that  you'll also take more damage when at  longer range from the NPC's so from this  we can take away a couple of things that  should be applied to your global event  build 1 we need weapons that excel at  close range and 2 we need to position  ourselves up close to the NPCs this is  where I see a lot of players falling  short  thanks to the main modifier of increased  close combat damage no one really has to  worry about the damage they're doing any  weapon will work up close so for now  let's remove that from the equation the  NPC extended range damage multiplier is  causing a lot of players to be to tempt  before they can even react but don't  jump straight into throwing extra points  into stamina as I've mentioned another  video stamina is a horrifically  inefficient step to focus on in 1.7  instead you should be looking at the  skills we have at our disposal and the  one that sticks out straight away is the  ballistic shield this will allow you to  tank a lot of those shots while you move  within range naturally to take full  advantage of the shield you want to  equip the d3 if in cease it but you  can't stop there with the threat  increase you'll be bringing all of the  enemy fire down on you so you'll need to  have constant flow of healing this is  where health on kill becomes an equally  important part of the build and as a  side note this will also help win  completing the complete without using  medical skills commendations as with all  of my build videos we'll be trying to  keep this as clear and concise as  possible  I'll never state that you need to match  everything I've added to the build and  instead the idea is for you to use this  as a starting point or a template for  your own build change things up and  personalize it for your style of play  this build consists of three piece d3  FNC one piece tactician one piece nomad  and the ninja bike messenger bag the  idea is to be able to tank the majority  of the damage with your ballistic shield  while constantly healing due to your  high dps health on kill setup you may  need to tweak the build slightly  depending on the content you're facing  but generally cover isn't required all  gear pieces have been rolled into  firearms and all major attributes into  skill taste or health on kill in the  first instance or skill power all mods  should be electronics with skill haste  as the attribute applying the above  should leave you with around 7k +  firearms 4k + electronics 50% skill  haste and 25% health on kill the  equipped skills are a ballistic shield  and overdose depending on the difficulty  of the enemies you're facing you may  want to change out overdose for booster  shot most of the time the health on kill  alone is enough to keep you topped up  the three talents old caller must are  critical so combat medic and on the move  combat medic is particularly important  as this will also heal your ballistic  shield when using a mid kit the last  talent one has none is optional you'll  spend a lot of time reloading with this  build so this talent will make your mags  feel like they last a little longer  between reloads it may actually be worth  losing some of the skill haste in order  to roll reload speed onto the holster  the primary weapon I'm using is the mp5  ST with the talents competent brutal and  responsive these talents work quite  nicely with the mp5 and will boost your  damage even further the secondary weapon  almost doesn't need to be looked at I  was using a second SMG with different  talents but it's a bit clunky changing  weapons with the shield er so I found I  never really used it in this example I'm  using the first wave m1 a with cool  headed and brutal but this was really  just to give me some range of the  situation called for it at the end of  this video I've included a cheat sheet  or a quick reference guide that sums up  this build and everything I've covered  check it out and see what you think I'll  leave you with a little bit of gameplay  now but if you'd like to see more of  this type of content subscribe to the  channel and leave a comment below thanks  [Music]  [Music]  morning agent of protein is down  requires assistance  you  [Music]

